    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96-a4">

                <pb facs="0240" n="168" xml:id="pg168"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 33.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. C. G. Boisselier to Mr. Sargent.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Borby near Eckernford</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your kind
                    lines from the 23d instant, which came into my hands this afternoon with the
                    accompanying papers, I beg leave to express my best thanks for your very prompt
                    attention to the case in question, and your clear explanation of the same, in
                    which my son Richard Werner, who has just returned to me from a trip in the
                    country, joins me.</p>
                <p>The papers for himself and for his brother, Casper Dethard, I have handed over to
                    him. He will return to the United States on the 30th of next month.</p>
                <p>I remain, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. G. BOISSELIER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
